+# Physical footprint and installed endpoint-slot authority
+
+Status: source-only correction after root attempts01/02 failed before any native
+fixture launched. Freeze05's exact277 files and source review are preserved in
+`history/source-freeze05`; both attempts remain unchanged. Root separately audited
+eight outer reaps, two original12-case/638-assertion evaluator results, no native
+fixtures and stable inputs/tools. This source preparation did not rerun or audit
+the attempts.
+
+The original graph requires each GPIO alias closure to equal its physical pin
+footprint (`resource_topology.py:294–303`). A lifecycle atom cannot be included as
+a GPIO footprint. The fixture now lists only the physical atom for each alias.
+The installed host parser requires each finite/standing proof's control claims
+to equal exactly the two hardware resources. It separately validates the slot as
+a distinct lifecycle atom on a driver node whose implementation digest equals the
+installed driver source digest. That driver must belong to both instance proofs
+and each participating alias's explicit transitive `requires` path. Containment
+and sibling paths do not establish slot authority.
+
+`InstalledPolicy.resources` adds that validated slot to the physical claims;
+`StandingStore.admit` uses this same resolver. Finite and standing reservation
+therefore both claim exactly the same three atoms in the original shared table.
+`mapping.resourceProof` retains the unmodified two-atom physical proof, while
+`mapping.claims` records all three actual claims. PAT artifact/compiler/selection
+and the mapping already bind the complete installation digest, including topology,
+generations and slotResource; no PAT schema or qualification claim is changed.
+The approved host plan explicitly requires a separate installed endpoint slot
+and distinguishes logical exclusive claims from quantitative capacity (lines78–85).
+
+The existing shared_authority control now asserts exact physical/actual sets for
+both families, rejects a service atom substituted as slot, a disconnected output
+alias and a driver source mismatch, and checks driver/service lifecycle exclusion
+while either family holds claims. The same twenty cases and all caps remain.
+Graph/schema, shared Journal, direct Registry guards and PAT source are unchanged.
+No additional row fields or physical/capacity eligibility are introduced.
+
+The fixed runner now exclusively creates host-attempt03 with distinct original
+qualification IDs ending in`:3`, verifies both prior result hashes before/after
+commands, and accurately retains previous-execution metadata. `revision-06.patch`
+records the exact delta. Actual owner death and other completion gates remain
+outstanding; no third attempt was executed during source preparation.
